zlib in ooSQLite
================

This directory holds zlib 1.3.2 (17 Feb 2026), https://zlib.net, from the
tag v1.3.2 of https://github.com/madler/zlib.  It is compiled into the ooSQLite
library for the compress and zipfile builtin extensions
(src/sqlite/extensions/compress.c and zipfile.c), so ooSQLite does not depend
on a zlib installed on the system.

The files are unchanged.  Only the ones needed for compress(), uncompress(),
deflate and inflate are here: the gz* files (except gzguts.h, which zutil.c
includes), infback.c, the build files, contrib/, examples/ and test/ are left
out.

zlib is built with Z_PREFIX (see Makefile.lin and Makefile.win), which gives
every external symbol a z_ prefix, so it cannot clash with another zlib loaded
into the same process.

The zlib license is in LICENSE.

To update: replace the files with those of the new release, update the version
above, rebuild and run the test suite (Tier 5F and 5G, section C14).
